<article class="env-lemma" id="021T">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/021T">Lemma <span data-tag="021T">34.7.9</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$ be a big fppf site containing $S$. Then $(\textit{Aff}/S)_{fppf}$ is a site. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let us show that $(\textit{Aff}/S)_{fppf}$ is a site. Reasoning as in the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/021C" data-tag="021C">34.4.9</a> it suffices to show that the collection of standard fppf coverings of affines satisfies properties (1), (2) and (3) of Sites, Definition <a href="/tag/00VH" data-tag="00VH">7.6.2</a>. This is clear since for example, given a standard fppf covering $\{ T_ i \to T\} _{i\in I}$ and for each $i$ we have a standard fppf covering $\{ T_{ij} \to T_ i\} _{j\in J_ i}$, then $\{ T_{ij} \to T\} _{i \in I, j\in J_ i}$ is a standard fppf covering because $\bigcup _{i\in I} J_ i$ is finite and each $T_{ij}$ is affine. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>